  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>I.<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>log</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>–</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>)</mo></math>, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>–</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>)</mo></math> is remaining concentration, decreases with passage of time.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>log</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>log</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>kt</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>.303</mo></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>log</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>.3030</mo></mrow></mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>slope</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>ve</mi></math><br />II. <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2.303</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">log</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mrow></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>log</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>.303</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>×</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>303</mn></mrow></mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math><br /><math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>×</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math><br />Plot of <math><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">log</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mrow></math> against 't' gives straight line through origin.<br />III. <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>0.693</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>;</mo></math> Half-life of first order reaction does not depend on initial concentration. Thus, graph of <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> against 'a' gives horizontal straight line.</p>",
